Here is my ill-fated attempt at making a 3x ascension streak:

Terry the Neutral Male Monk, 12/17/06

10:00 AM
It is morning; it is time for NetHack.
I go down the list again; I choose a Monk.
My starting spell is protection; not sleep. I am a bit worried.
The first few levels are uneventful. I enter the Mines on DL 3.
This level is lit. The gnomes are no match for my kung-fu.
Second level is lit too. Nothing much here.
I fall through a trapdoor. Minetown.

10:15 AM
The shops don't have anything of interest. I buy seven candles from
Isack, and leave.
On the ground, I find a sack. Not a bag of holding, but it will
suffice.
A few levels down, in the main dungeon, I accidentally push a boulder
into a corner.
The up-staircase was there. No choice now but to continue.
A dwarf leaves a broad pick. It welds itself to my hand. I manage to
uncurse it in a fountain.
With my throughly rusty broad pick, I dig downwards. A group of dingos
assaults me.
I whack them with the pick, then realize that I lost my weaponless
conduct.
I continue.

10:30 AM
I dig, and fall into a big room. There are two staircases up, and one
down. I run for the up staircase.
Not the Oracle level, but Sokoban. I recover some lost hitpoints and
complete the first level.
Returning downstairs, I am mobbed by monsters. I manage to kill some,
but am forced to retreat.
I complete the second level of Sokoban, and return downstairs.
Fortunately, I have AC -7 with protection.
Again, I am forced to retreat. I finish the third level of Sokoban, and
return to the melee.
A Grey-elf, equipped with speed boots, reaches me. His elven broadsword
cuts deeply into me, and I once again retreat.
I begin the fourth and final level. It is the bag of holding reward.
The amulet of reflection would have been more useful to me, but it is a
good prize nonetheless.
A black unicorn attacks me, and I slay it. I take the unicorn horn, and
return to the big room.

10:45 AM
I do not manage to slay the Grey-elf. I return to finish Sokoban.
A lucky shot with a wand of cold saves me from death by soldier ant.
Going back downstairs, I shoot the Grey-elf with the wand of cold and
then bash him to death.
I pick up his speed boots, quaff a potion of healing, then finish off
the rest of the monsters.
Time to continue downstairs.
By now I have collected a wand of digging, a wand of cold, a wand of
fire, and two wands of striking.
Less useful are a wand of make invisible, a wand of slow monster, a
wand of create monster, and a wand of cancellation.
I've learned drain life; the other spellbooks are too much for my INT
10 monk to comprehend.

11:00 AM
I wander through the dungeon until DL 17, when I decide to dig my way
down.
I reach the titan version of Medusa's, and zap a wand of digging.
There is a maze level here; I am on the left side. A minotaur is
directly north of me.
I make a dash for the right; I hear doors open; a master lich spawns
before me.
He weakens me with a few spells, but I ignore it; I reach the space
adjacent to the drawbridge and burn Elbereth.
The minotaur comes to two spaces from me; I cannot finish it off from a
distance. I break the wand of create monster.
This buys me more time. I wait, and occasionally hit the master lich.
When the minotaur comes inside my lines of fire, I cast drain life.
I run out of mana, and resort to throwing darts and shuriken.
Eventually it manages to come right next to me; I kill it. It never
even touched me.

11:30 AM
It is turn 5827 and I am set to enter the castle. Unfortunately, I do
not have an instrument.
I accidentally walk into the water and blank my scrolls.
Finally I decide to use the wand of striking on the drawbridge. I
freeze the water diagonally adjacent to it.
Soldiers come out; the master lich pesters me. I slay a few while the
lich creates monsters all the while.
My health is critically low. I am hit by a bolt of lightning. I take
out my last potion of healing and quaff it.
The lich summons a couatl, a master mind flayer and an elf-lord
adjacent to me. A cockatrice is two square away.
I attack the soldier with the wand of lightning, which is quickly
changing owners. Finally I decide to cancel it.
The elf-lord and couatl beat up on me.
Do you want your possessions identified?

Terry, neutral male human Monk






